#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - cohomcalg 0.32 C++11 user-defined literal concat
# Source package: cohomcalg/0.32
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-cohomcalg-0.32-cpp11-literal-concat
trigger_tool:           clang++|make
phase:                  compilation
error_signature:        invalid suffix on literal; C++11 requires a space between literal and identifier

severity:               2
category:               portability|compiler|clang
match_keywords:         C++11, user-defined literal, string literal, macro, P_VALUE_FMT, clang++, strict parsing, old C code, space between literal and identifier, string concat, legacy code, GCC

title:                  C++11 user-defined-literal error: string literal immediately followed by a macro identifier needs a space

root_cause:             >
    C++11 introduces user-defined string literals: a string literal immediately followed by an
    identifier is parsed as a user-defined-literal suffix. Legacy C/C++ code that concatenates a
    string literal with a macro identifier (e.g. `" "P_VALUE_FMT" "` where P_VALUE_FMT expands to
    a format specifier) compiles fine under old GCC's lenient parsing, but clang++ (strict C++11
    parsing) rejects it:
        error: invalid suffix on literal; C++11 requires a space between literal and identifier
    In cohomcalg 0.32 this hit source/polylib_mod/matrix.c:153 `value_print(Dst," "P_VALUE_FMT" ",*p++);`
    The fix is to insert a space between the closing quote and the macro identifier:
    `" " P_VALUE_FMT " "` (macro expansion then concatenates as before).

affected_scope:         Any legacy C/C++ (especially polyhedral/numeric libraries with printf-style
                        format macro concatenation) adapted with clang++ on OHOS; GCC used to be lenient.

verification_cmd:       |
  cd <worktree> && make -j1 CC=clang++ LD=clang++ && ./bin/cohomcalg --integrated --nomonomfile bin/dP1.in

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           space-between-literal-and-macro
rec_description: >
    In the source (or a portability patch), add a space between a string literal and any
    macro identifier that immediately follows it: `"fmt"MACRO` -> `"fmt" MACRO`.
    The macro expansion is unaffected (whitespace is dropped during token concatenation).
rec_command:            |
  sed -i 's/" "P_VALUE_FMT" "/" " P_VALUE_FMT " "/' source/polylib_mod/matrix.c
rec_auto_fix:           true
rec_impl:               patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      compile-as-C99-for-legacy-c
fallback_description:   If the offending translation unit is pure C and the build system allows it,
                        compile that .c file with a C compiler (or -std=gnu99) instead of C++ mode.
fallback_command:       make CC=clang LD=clang
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual

forbid_1_pattern:       ignore the error with -Wno-error or -Wno-reserved-user-defined-literal
forbid_1_reason:        The construct is ill-formed in C++11; suppressing the warning does not make
                        the parse well-defined and other compilers/toolchains may still reject it.
forbid_1_consequence:   Build succeeds locally but fails on stricter toolchains; UB / misparse risk.

similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

